      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the length of the tunnel given the speed of the train and the time it takes for the train to completely exit the tunnel.\n\n### Step-by-Step Reasoning:\n\n1. **Convert the speed of the train to miles per minute:**\n   The train's speed is given as 60 miles per hour. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert the speed to miles per minute:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed in miles per minute} = \\frac{60 \\text{ miles per hour}}{60 \\text{ minutes per hour}} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the total distance traveled by the train in 3 minutes:**\n   The train exits the tunnel exactly 3 minutes after the front of the train enters the tunnel. Therefore, the total distance traveled by the train in this time is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute} \\times 3 \\text{ minutes} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Set up the equation to find the length of the tunnel:**\n   The total distance traveled by the train includes the length of the tunnel plus the length of the train. Let \\( L \\) be the length of the tunnel. The total distance is the sum of the length of the tunnel and the length of the train:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = L + \\text{Length of the train}\n   \\]\n   The length of the train is given as 1 mile. Therefore, we can write:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ miles} = L + 1 \\text{ mile}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for the length of the tunnel \\( L \\):**\n   \\[\n   L = 3 \\text{ miles} - 1 \\text{ mile} = 2 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\nThe length of the tunnel is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) miles.",
