      "text": "To determine the length of the tunnel, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1. **Convert the train's speed to miles per minute:**\n   The train's speed is 60 miles per hour. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert the speed to miles per minute:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed of the train} = \\frac{60 \\text{ miles}}{60 \\text{ minutes}} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the distance the train travels in 3 minutes:**\n   The train travels at a speed of 1 mile per minute. In 3 minutes, the train travels:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance traveled in 3 minutes} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute} \\times 3 \\text{ minutes} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the length of the tunnel:**\n   When the front of the train enters the tunnel, it travels the length of the tunnel plus 3 miles (the distance the train has traveled). When the tail of the train exits the tunnel, the front of the train has traveled the length of the tunnel plus 3 miles. Since the front of the train travels 3 miles to the point where the tail of the train exits the tunnel, the length of the tunnel is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length of the tunnel} = \\text{Distance traveled by the train} - 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n   The distance the train travels is the length of the tunnel plus 3 miles. Since the train's speed is 1 mile per minute, the distance it travels in 3 minutes is 3 miles. Therefore, the length of the tunnel is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length of the tunnel} = \\text{Distance traveled by the train} - 3 \\text{ miles} = (\\text{Length of the tunnel} + 3 \\text{ miles}) - 3 \\text{ miles} = \\text{Length of the tunnel}\n   \\]\n   This equation simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length of the tunnel} = \\text{Length of the tunnel}\n   \\]\n   However, we need to subtract the 3 miles that the train has traveled to reach the point where the tail exits. Therefore, the length of the tunnel is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length of the tunnel} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length of the tunnel is \\(\\boxed{3}\\) miles.",
